-d81-a2-2026-11-12/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Cicero spoke highly of this city and appears to have been its patron. Before that, the city struck its own coins and sided with Carthage after the battle of Cannae, allied with Capua."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a2-2026-11-12: checker card_fact_checker:teaser-check-001 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a2-2026-11-12/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Cicero spoke highly of the city [S2]; Cicero appears to have been its patron [S2]; it was a city [S1]; the events of the second sentence came before Cicero''s time [S1, S2]; the city struck its own coins [S1]; it sided with Carthage after the battle of Cannae [S1]; it was allied with Capua [S1]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-shorts-d81-a2-2026-11-12: verifier card_web_verifier:teaser-verify-001 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-shorts-d81-a2-2026-11-12/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Cicero spoke highly of this city. [SUPPORTED: https://www.thelatinlibrary.com/cicero/fam13.shtml]; Cicero appears to have been the city''s patron. [SUPPORTED: https://www.thelatinlibrary.com/cicero/fam13.shtml]; The city struck its own coins. [SUPPORTED: http://snible.org/coins/hn/campania.html]; The coinage and the siding with Carthage came before Cicero''s time. [SUPPORTED: http://snible.org/coins/hn/campania.html]; The city sided with Carthage. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/From_the_Founding_of_the_City/Book_22]; The city sided with Carthage after the battle of Cannae. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/From_the_Founding_of_the_City/Book_22]; The city was allied with Capua when it sided with Carthage. [SUPPORTED: http://snible.org/coins/hn/campania.html]"}]'::jsonb),
